<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bantry Bay</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bantry Bay is a long inlet of the Atlantic on the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-cork">County Cork</a> in south-west Ireland. In December 1796 a French expedition under General Hoche, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theobald-wolfe-tone">Wolfe Tone</a> on board, reached the bay to support a rising of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/society-of-united-irishmen">United Irishmen</a>, but storms scattered the fleet and prevented any landing. An earlier French fleet had fought an English squadron there in 1689.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bantry-bay.jpg" alt="Bantry Bay" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mike Searle · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bantry_Town_and_Bay_from_Sheskin_-_geograph.org.uk_-_504839.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
